{% block user %}Aggregated single cells into {{ n_obs }} pseudobulk profiles by summing raw counts within each sample{% if params.get('groups_col') %} and {{ params.get('groups_col') }} group{% endif %}, ready for cross-condition differential expression.{% endblock %}

{% block methods %}Single-cell raw counts were aggregated into pseudobulk profiles by summing counts within each sample{% if params.get('groups_col') %} and {{ params.get('groups_col') }} group{% endif %} using decoupler (mode='{{ params.get('mode', 'sum') }}'), following Badia-i-Mompel et al. [badia_decoupler_2022]. Pseudobulk profiles derived from fewer than {{ params.get('min_cells', 10) }} cells were discarded, yielding {{ n_obs }} pseudobulk samples across {{ n_vars }} genes. Aggregating to the biological-replicate level prior to differential expression preserves sample-level variance and controls false-positive inflation (Squair et al. 2021).{% endblock %}
